MECHANISM (lead, verify in tree):
  store_screen.dart:187  onPressed: boot ? _escapeToHome : () => Get.back()
  `boot` = widget.autoOpened, and autoOpened is FALSE on this entry, so Back does a plain
  Get.back() with nothing beneath it on a cold deep-link open.
  On the HEALTHY path the screen survives because the slug branch relocates the user
  (store_controller.dart:818 setStoreAddressToUserAddress) and Home is built underneath;
  on the FAILURE path that never runs, so the pop lands on an uninitialised/!hasData route.

RELATED (separate, pre-existing): route_helper.dart:1530 `_storePage()` does
  Get.arguments ?? StoreScreen(... autoOpened: Get.parameters['auto_opened'] == 'true')
and single_store_hero_view.dart:137-144 passes BOTH `auto_opened=true` in the URL AND a
non-null `arguments: StoreScreen(store: store, fromModule: true)` (no autoOpened). The
non-null arguments wins, so autoOpened is silently dropped and `boot` is effectively
ALWAYS false app-wide -> the `if (boot)` "back to home" escape link (store_screen.dart:203-208)
is dead code today. ('back_to_home' also has no translation entry.)

